{
  "$comment": [
    "Coverage of the pinned upstream surface (upstream/openapi.json and upstream/sdk/), checked by test/node/upstream-coverage.test.ts.",
    "operations: every upstream OpenAPI operation, keyed by operationId, in exactly one state:",
    "  wrapped  - served by the cmux VM endpoints named in `by` (operationIds in openapi.json);",
    "  planned  - not wrapped yet; `bead` names the task that will wrap it. A distinct state from denied: the slice that wraps it flips it to wrapped;",
    "  denied   - deliberately never wrapped; `reason` says why.",
    "sdk: every public method of every class the upstream SDK declares, as Class.method; cli: every command the upstream CLI exports.",
    "Each maps to the upstream operations it calls (and so inherits their state), or is denied or local (no request) with a reason."
  ],
  "operations": {
    "get_background_request": {
      "status": "denied",
      "reason": "Transport detail of the provider client: a request is backgrounded only when the caller sends the background-after header, which cmux VM never does, and background request ids are account-wide, so they cannot be scoped to a tenant."
    },
